      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i've also seen some old notes saying there are physiological differences in how different groups experience things like pain or inflammation. like, is there any actual clinical basis for the idea that certain races might have higher pain thresholds or require different dosages for anesthesia? just trying to clarify what's evidence-based vs just old stereotypes i've heard.",
