      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's an interesting distinction between genetics and culture. since you mentioned specific studies regarding West African or Asian descent, does that mean when we're in a clinical setting, it's actually more 'accurate' to assume those groups might be more resistant to certain meds? like, should a doctor be cautious about under-treating pain in those specific populations because of those higher opioid levels you mentioned? i want to make sure i understand how this actually applies to real-world bedside decisions.",
